                                "sense_id": "686d83f2-c3d3-3ceb-a134-e1ac5b73ed19",
                                "text": "The Constitution of the United States permits the suffrage of women. . . . Under it legally constituted women—as to age, freedom from criminalness, etc.—may vote for all officers from president to township supervisor."
